# Initial Setup's Radio Calibration page, ported from GCSViews/ConfigurationView/ConfigRadioInput.cs.
#
# The claims, each read from the application's facts and, for the vehicle, its own echo:
#
# * Activate (ConfigRadioInput.cs:42-177) binds roll, pitch, throttle and yaw through RCMAP_* and
#   adds each one's channel to its label, binds BAR5-BAR16 to channels 5-16, and asks for
#   RC_CHANNELS at 2 Hz; the sixteen bars show what the receiver reports.
# * On a copter the four Reverse boxes are bound to RCn_REVERSED and then hidden
#   (ConfigRadioInput.cs:140-147, 167-174), and the elevon group is hidden (:126-137). No Reverse
#   box can be clicked on SITL's copter, so none is here: the test asserts they are bound and
#   hidden. The Reverse write and its restore - RC1_REVERSED written 1 with the bar mirrored, then
#   written 0 - are proven through the real link to a scripted plane in config/radio.rs's
#   a_reverse_box_writes_its_parameter_and_mirrors_its_bar, with SWITCH_ENABLE's Dip Switch step
#   in the_dip_switches_are_disabled_before_the_reverse_is_written.
# * Calibrate Radio's conversation (ConfigRadioInput.cs:197-406), step by step: its messages in
#   order, the button's text at each, RC_CHANNELS at 10 Hz while it runs and back to the link's
#   rate once it is saved, the minimum and maximum the loop folds in, the trims, and the summary.
#   SITL's RC inputs are static - ch1-8 read 1500 1500 1000 1500 1800 1000 1000 1800 and nothing
#   is reported above 8 (ArduPilot's AP_RCProtocol_UDP::set_default_pwm_input_values) - so no
#   channel moves, every minimum equals its maximum, and the C# writes nothing: its save wants
#   rcmin < rcmax (ConfigRadioInput.cs:363-365). The test asserts exactly that - no write, and
#   RCn_MIN, _MAX and _TRIM unchanged on the vehicle. The forced writes of a swept radio are
#   proven through the real link in a_swept_radio_writes_min_max_and_trim_forced_then_the_summary.
# * Bind DSM2 sends MAV_CMD_START_RX_PAIR with 0 in its second parameter, which SITL accepts, and
#   the C# then says to put the transmitter in bind mode (ConfigRadioInput.cs:471-482).
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760 started from tools/sitl/params/copter.parm, which sets
# RC1-8_MIN 1000, _MAX 2000 and _TRIM 1500 and leaves RCMAP_* and RCn_REVERSED at the firmware's
# defaults (1 2 3 4, and 0). Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/config-radio.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760
#
# Nothing this test does changes a parameter, so a run that stops half way leaves the vehicle as
# it found it.

screen params
window 1600x1200
settle 6

# Initial Setup lists the page once every parameter is in (InitialSetup.cs:211, isConnected &&
# gotAllParams), and here parameters are downloaded when asked for.
click param-download
settle 15
expect params.held > 1000
expect params.value.RC1_MIN 1000
expect params.value.RC1_MAX 2000
expect params.value.RC1_TRIM 1500
expect params.value.RC3_TRIM 1500
expect params.value.RC1_REVERSED 0
expect config.radio.active false

# The page is under Mandatory Hardware, which choosing opens.
click tab-setup
click setup-page-ConfigMandatory
click setup-page-ConfigRadioInput
settle 2
expect setup.page ConfigRadioInput
expect config.radio.active true
expect config.radio.enabled true
expect config.radio.firmware ArduCopter2
expect config.radio.map 1,2,3,4
expect config.radio.stream 2

# The bars: each stick's bound to its RCMAP channel and labelled with it, the rest to 5-16.
expect config.radio.bar.roll.channel 1
expect config.radio.bar.roll.text ~ Roll (rc1)
expect config.radio.bar.roll 1500
expect config.radio.bar.pitch.channel 2
expect config.radio.bar.pitch.text ~ Pitch (rc2)
expect config.radio.bar.pitch 1500
expect config.radio.bar.throttle.channel 3
expect config.radio.bar.throttle.text ~ Throttle (rc3)
expect config.radio.bar.throttle 1000
expect config.radio.bar.yaw.channel 4
expect config.radio.bar.yaw.text ~ Yaw (rc4)
expect config.radio.bar.yaw 1500
expect config.radio.bar.5.channel 5
expect config.radio.bar.5.text ~ Radio 5
expect config.radio.bar.5 1800
expect config.radio.bar.6 1000
expect config.radio.bar.7 1000
expect config.radio.bar.8 1800
expect config.radio.bar.9 0
expect config.radio.bar.16.channel 16
expect config.radio.bar.16 0
# Nothing reversed, and no red lines before a calibration.
expect config.radio.bar.roll.reverse false
expect config.radio.bar.roll.min 0

# The Reverse boxes, bound to RCn_REVERSED on the RCMAP channels and hidden on a copter.
expect config.radio.reverse.1.param RC1_REVERSED
expect config.radio.reverse.1 unchecked
expect config.radio.reverse.1.enabled true
expect config.radio.reverse.1.visible false
expect config.radio.reverse.2.param RC2_REVERSED
expect config.radio.reverse.2.visible false
expect config.radio.reverse.3.param RC3_REVERSED
expect config.radio.reverse.3.visible false
expect config.radio.reverse.4.param RC4_REVERSED
expect config.radio.reverse.4.visible false
expect config.radio.elevons.visible false
expect config.radio.button Calibrate Radio
expect config.radio.message none

# Calibrate Radio: the first message; the button's text is unchanged until it is dismissed.
click radio-calibrate
settle 1
expect config.radio.message ~ Ensure your transmitter is on and receiver is powered and connected
expect config.radio.message ~ Ensure your motor does not have power/no props!!!
expect config.radio.button Calibrate Radio
click radio-message-ok
settle 1
# RC_CHANNELS at 10 Hz, the button's new text, and the second message.
expect config.radio.stream 10
expect config.radio.button Click when Done
expect config.radio.message ~ Click OK and move all RC sticks and switches to their
click radio-message-ok
settle 2
# The loop: every channel folded into its minimum and maximum, and the bars' red lines on them.
expect config.radio.running true
expect config.radio.message none
expect config.radio.min.1 1500
expect config.radio.max.1 1500
expect config.radio.min.3 1000
expect config.radio.max.3 1000
expect config.radio.min.5 1800
expect config.radio.max.8 1800
expect config.radio.min.9 0
expect config.radio.max.16 0
expect config.radio.bar.roll.min 1500
expect config.radio.bar.roll.max 1500
expect config.radio.bar.throttle.min 1000
expect config.radio.bar.5.max 1800
# Static sticks: nothing the save would write.
expect config.radio.writes none

# Click when Done: the loop ends, channel 1 read a real pulse, so the sticks-centred message.
click radio-calibrate
settle 1
expect config.radio.running false
expect config.radio.button Completed
expect config.radio.message ~ Ensure all your sticks are centered and throttle is down
click radio-message-ok
settle 2
# The trims, each reading constrained into its range; nothing to write; RC_CHANNELS back at the
# rate the link asked for on connecting; and the summary, with only its rule under the heading.
expect config.radio.trim.1 1500
expect config.radio.trim.3 1000
expect config.radio.trim.5 1800
expect config.radio.trim.9 0
expect config.radio.writes none
expect config.radio.pending 0
expect config.radio.write none
expect config.radio.stream 4
expect config.radio.button Saving
expect config.radio.message.title Radio
expect config.radio.message ~ Here are the detected radio options
expect config.radio.message ~ Normal values are around 1100 | 1900
expect config.radio.message ~ ---------------
click radio-message-ok
settle 1
expect config.radio.button Completed
expect config.radio.message none

# The vehicle holds what it held.
expect params.value.RC1_MIN 1000
expect params.value.RC1_MAX 2000
expect params.value.RC1_TRIM 1500
expect params.value.RC3_MIN 1000
expect params.value.RC3_TRIM 1500
expect params.value.RC8_MAX 2000

# Bind DSM2: START_RX_PAIR with 0, accepted, and the C#'s message.
click radio-bind-dsm2
settle 3
expect config.radio.bind START_RX_PAIR 0 accepted
expect config.radio.message Put the transmitter in bind mode. Receiver is waiting.
click radio-message-ok
settle 1
expect config.radio.message none

# Choosing another page deactivates this one (BackstageView.cs:453-464).
click setup-page-ConfigMandatory
settle 1
expect config.radio.active false
